description:
## Problem
service_locator.dart (657 LOC) has nested Future.microtask at lines 94-115:

```dart
Future.microtask(() {           // Outer
  if (locator.isRegistered<VoiceService>()) {
    simpleTTSService.setVoiceServiceUpdateCallback(...);
    Future.microtask(() {       // Inner — fires after indeterminate delay
      if (locator.isRegistered<VoiceSessionBloc>()) {
        simpleTTSService.setGetCurrentGenerationCallback(...);
      }
    });
  }
});
```

The nesting exists because VoiceService and VoiceSessionBloc are registered lazily.
The inner microtask fires at an indeterminate time. This is fragile.

## Solution
Move callback wiring to a dedicated post-registration step:
- After all services are registered, run a single wiring phase
- Or: wire callbacks in the VoiceSessionBloc constructor (which already has access to services)
- The bloc constructor already wires generation callbacks at lines 321-327

## Acceptance Criteria
- No nested Future.microtask in service_locator.dart
- All callbacks still wired correctly
- flutter analyze: 0 errors
- Estimated LOC reduction: ~20
